  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Hilton–Milner theorem",
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the Hilton–Milner theorem: for k ≥ 2 and n > 2k, a nontrivial intersecting family of k-subsets of an n-set (no element lies in all members) has at most C(n−1, k−1) − C(n−k−1, k−1) + 1 members, and this bound is attained. Intersecting is Mathlib's Set.Intersecting. Mathlib contains the Erdős–Ko–Rado theorem but not this result.",
